                loading="lazy"
                style="width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; border-radius:8px;"
              />
            </a>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 8: Western Art Today -->
        <div class="section-heading-with-line">
          <h2>Western Art Today</h2>
        </div>

        <p>Contemporary Western art continues to evolve.</p>

        <p>Some artists still work within the heroic tradition, painting riders against sunsets or dramatic frontier scenes. Others explore modern ranch life, environmental tension, cultural identity, or the psychological weight of Western spaces.</p>

        <p>The subject has expanded, but the core themes remain:</p>

        <ul style="list-style:disc; padding-left:1.5rem; margin:1rem 0 1.5rem;">
          <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Isolation and community</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Hardship and endurance</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Freedom and consequence</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Land as both refuge and challenge</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Western art is no longer just about history. It is about the ongoing meaning of the West.</p>

        <!-- SECTION 9: Explore Western Themes in Practice -->
        <div class="section-heading-with-line">
          <h2>Explore Western Themes in Practice</h2>
        </div>

        <p>These thematic collections draw from the full body of Western work — each revealing a different facet of frontier life, mythology, and emotional truth.</p>

        <div class="theme-grid" style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap:0.75rem 1.5rem; margin:1.5rem 0 2.5rem;">
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=cowboys-and-horses&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">Cowboys and Horses</a>
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=hardship-sorrow&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">Hardship & Sorrow</a>
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=frontier-women&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">Frontier Women</a>
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=law-outlaws&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">Law & Outlaws</a>
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=dust-thunder&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">Dust & Thunder</a>
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=firelight-shadow&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">Firelight & Shadow</a>
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=love-goodbye&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">Love & Goodbye</a>
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=the-chase&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">The Chase</a>
          <a href="/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/Western-Cowboy-Portraits/Color?theme=sketches-of-legends&view=grid" style="color:#8b5a2b; text-decoration:underline;">Sketches of Legends</a>
